tures this way gives the list 80, 81, 81, 81, 82. Therefore, the median high temperature is 81&deg;F. Choice B is incorrect. The mean high temperature is <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"the fraction with numerator 81, plus 80, plus 81, plus 81, plus 82, and denominator 5, equals, the fraction 405 over 5, which equals 81\"></span>. Choice C is incorrect. The mode is the value that occurs the greatest number of times. For the set of high temperatures shown,&nbsp;81 is the value that occurs 3 times, and therefore, 81&deg;F is the <!--StartFragment-->mode of the high temperatures<!--EndFragment-->.</p></p>\n"}},"createDate":1691007959634,"updateDate":1691007959634}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959634, 1691007959634),
    ($SATQ$8705ecba$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$028060-DC$SATQ$, $SATQ$disclosed$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q.B.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Percentages$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 3, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p class="stem_paragraph ">The cost of a certain shirt is $20 before a 5% sales tax is added. What is the total cost, including sales tax, to purchase the shirt?</p>
$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"a","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">$20.05</p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">$20.50</p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">$21.00</p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">$25.00</p>\n"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["C"]$SATQ$::jsonb, NULL, $SATQ$<p>Choice C is correct. The total cost to purchase the shirt is the $20 cost of the shirt plus the 5% sales tax. The value of the 5% sales tax on the $20 shirt is equivalent to<span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/8705ecba/img_000_1b543ca8.png" alt="0 point 0 5 times 20 dollars"></span>, or $1. Therefore, the total cost to purchase the shirt is <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/8705ecba/img_001_568a7646.png" alt="20 dollars plus 1 dollar"></span>, or $21.<p>Choice A is incorrect and may result from neglecting to multiply by $20 when finding the value of the sales tax. Choice B is incorrect and may result from dividing by 10, instead of by 100, and then neglecting to multiply by $20 when finding the sales tax. Choice D is incorrect and may result from interpreting the sales tax of 5% as $5.</p></p>
$SATQ$, false, 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$Multiple Choice$SATQ$, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ${"questionId":"8705ecba","external_id":null,"disclosed_item_id":"028060-DC","source":"disclosed","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"Q","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill_cd":"Q.B.","skill_desc":"Percentages","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":3,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">The cost of a certain shirt is $20 before a 5% sales tax is added. What is the total cost, including sales tax, to purchase the shirt?</p>\n","answerOptions":[{"id":"a","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">$20.05</p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">$20.50</p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">$21.00</p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">$25.00</p>\n"}],"keys":null,"correct_answer":["C"],"rationale":"<p>Choice C is correct. The total cost to purchase the shirt is the $20 cost of the shirt plus the 5% sales tax. The value of the 5% sales tax on the $20 shirt is equivalent to<span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/8705ecba/img_000_1b543ca8.png\" alt=\"0 point 0 5 times 20 dollars\"></span>, or $1. Therefore, the total cost to purchase the shirt is <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/8705ecba/img_001_568a7646.png\" alt=\"20 dollars plus 1 dollar\"></span>, or $21.<p>Choice A is incorrect and may result from neglecting to multiply by $20 when finding the value of the sales tax. Choice B is incorrect and may result from dividing by 10, instead of by 100, and then neglecting to multiply by $20 when finding the sales tax. Choice D is incorrect and may result from interpreting the sales tax of 5% as $5.</p></p>\n","answer_style":"Multiple Choice","section":"Math","image_count":2,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1691007959622,"pPcc":"SAT#Q","questionId":"8705ecba","skill_cd":"Q.B.","score_band_range_cd":3,"skill_desc":"Percentages","createDate":1691007959622,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","ibn":"028060-DC","external_id":null,"primary_class_cd":"Q","uId":"27477198-cbe5-43dd-b80a-b93bfae4fc4f","difficulty":"E"},"raw_detail":{"item_id":"028060-DC","section":"Math","prompt":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">The cost of a certain shirt is $20 before a 5% sales tax is added. What is the total cost, including sales tax, to purchase the shirt?</p>\n","answer":{"style":"Multiple Choice","choices":{"a":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">$20.05</p>\n"},"b":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">$20.50</p>\n"},"c":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">$21.00</p>\n"},"d":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">$25.00</p>\n"}},"correct_choice":"c","rationale":"<p>Choice C is correct. The total cost to purchase the shirt is the $20 cost of the shirt plus the 5% sales tax. The value of the 5% sales tax on the $20 shirt is equivalent to<span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"0 point 0 5 times 20 dollars\"></span>, or $1. Therefore, the total cost to purchase the shirt is <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"20 dollars plus 1 dollar\"></span>, or $21.<p>Choice A is incorrect and may result from neglecting to multiply by $20 when finding the value of the sales tax. Choice B is incorrect and may result from dividing by 10, instead of by 100, and then neglecting to multiply by $20 when finding the sales tax. Choice D is incorrect and may result from interpreting the sales tax of 5% as $5.</p></p>\n"}},"createDate":1691007959622,"updateDate":1691007959622}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959622, 1691007959622),
    ($SATQ$8736334b$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$026304-DC$SATQ$, $SATQ$disclosed$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q.C.$SATQ$, $SATQ$One-variable data: Distributions and measures of center and spread$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<div xmlns="http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/apip/apipv1p0/qtiitem/imsqti_v2p1" class="stimulus_reference ">
        <p class="standalone_statement style:1 ">
          <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/8736334b/img_000_126f841d.png" alt="Data set A consists of the 5 numbers: 72, 73, 73, 76, and 76. Data set B consists of the 5 numbers: 61, 64, 74, 85, and x."></span>
