$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p class="stem_paragraph ">Data set A and data set B each contain 5 numbers. If the mean of data set A is equal to the mean of data set B, what is the value of <span class="italic">x </span>?</p>
$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"a","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph block_choice\">77</p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph block_choice\">85</p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph block_choice\">86</p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph block_choice\">95</p>\n"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["C"]$SATQ$::jsonb, NULL, $SATQ$<p>Choice C is correct. The mean of a data set is found by dividing the sum of the values in the data set by the number of values in the data set. Therefore, the mean of data set A is <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/8736334b/img_001_c40edd7c.png" alt="the fraction with numerator 72, plus 73, plus 73, plus 76, plus 76, and denominator 5"></span>, which simplifies to 74. The mean of data set B is represented by the equation <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/8736334b/img_002_04649bbe.png" alt="the fraction with numerator 61, plus 64, plus 74, plus 85, plus x, and denominator 5"></span>, or <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/8736334b/img_003_ff1bd750.png" alt="the fraction with numerator 284 plus x, and denominator 5"></span>. It&rsquo;s given that the mean of data set A is equal to the mean of data set B. Therefore, the equation <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/8736334b/img_004_30a1f0fb.png" alt="74 equals, the fraction with numerator 284 plus x, and denominator 5"></span> can be used to solve for <span class="italic">x</span>. Multiplying both sides of this equation by 5 yields <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/8736334b/img_005_366e497a.png" alt="370 equals, 284 plus x"></span>. Subtracting 284 from both sides of this equation yields <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/8736334b/img_006_c331a744.png" alt="86 equals x"></span>.<p>Choices A, B, and D are incorrect and may result from calculation errors.</p></p>
