s 90,000 \"></span> meters. Since 1 hour is equal to 60 minutes and 1 minute is equal to 60 seconds, it follows that 1 hour is equal to <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"60 times 60, equals 3,600 \"></span> seconds. Now <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"the fraction 90 kilometers over 1 hour\"></span> is equal to <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"the fraction 90,000 meters over 3,600 seconds\"></span>, which reduces to <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"the fraction 25 meters over 1 second\"></span> or 25 meters per second.<p>Choices B, C, and D are incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>\n"}},"createDate":1691007959624,"updateDate":1691007959624}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959624, 1691007959624),
