<p style="text-align: left;">One of these participants will be selected at random. What is the probability of selecting a participant from group A, given that the participant is at least 10 years of age?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"03edd3fd-773b-4956-aa2d-e94521d089d7","content":"<p><math alttext=\"five eighteenths\"><mfrac>\n\t<mn>5</mn>\n\t<mn>18</mn>\n</mfrac>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"259b5243-9745-45ce-8068-903e4e193d44","content":"<p><math alttext=\"five twelfths\"><mfrac>\n\t<mn>5</mn>\n\t<mn>12</mn>\n</mfrac>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"af601e26-46c4-4acf-bf24-6de5cbf8a6e0","content":"<p><math alttext=\"StartFraction 17 Over 30 EndFraction\"><mfrac>\n\t<mn>17</mn>\n\t<mn>30</mn>\n</mfrac>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"9b7faf67-be5d-40b8-9fd4-8114be71ac45","content":"<p><math alttext=\"five sixths\"><mfrac>\n\t<mn>5</mn>\n\t<mn>6</mn>\n</mfrac>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["259b5243-9745-45ce-8068-903e4e193d44"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is correct. Since the participant will be selected at random, the probability of selecting a participant from group A, given that the participant is at least <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="10"><mn>10</mn></math>&nbsp;years of age, is equal to the number of participants from group A who are at least&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="10"><mn>10</mn></math>&nbsp;years of age divided by the total number of participants who are at least&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="10"><mn>10</mn></math> years of age. Based on the table, in group A, there are <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="17"><mn>17</mn></math>&nbsp;participants who are <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="10"><mn>10</mn></math>&ndash;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="19"><mn>19</mn></math> years of age and <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="8"><mn>8</mn></math> participants who are&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="20 plus"><mn>20</mn><mo>+</mo></math>&nbsp;years of age. Therefore, there are a total of&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="17 plus 8"><mn>17</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn></math>, or&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="25"><mn>25</mn></math>, participants in group A who are at least&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="10"><mn>10</mn></math> years of age. Based on the table, of the total number of participants, there are <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="30"><mn>30</mn></math> participants who are <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="10"><mn>10</mn></math>&ndash;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="19"><mn>19</mn></math> years of age and <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="30"><mn>30</mn></math> participants who are <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="20 plus"><mn>20</mn><mo>+</mo></math> years of age. Therefore, a total of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="30 plus 30"><mn>30</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>30</mn></math>, or <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="60"><mn>60</mn></math>, of the participants are at least <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="10"><mn>10</mn></math> years of age. Thus, the probability of selecting a participant from group A, given that the participant is at least <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="10"><mn>10</mn></math> years of age, is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="StartFraction 25 Over 60 EndFraction"><mfrac><mn>25</mn><mn>60</mn></mfrac></math>, or <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="five twelfths"><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>12</mn></mfrac></math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect. This is the number of participants from group A who are at least <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="10"><mn>10</mn></math> years of age divided by the total number of participants, rather than divided by the number of participants who are at least <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="10"><mn>10</mn></math> years of age.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is incorrect. This is the probability of randomly selecting a participant from group A, given that the participant is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="10"><mn>10</mn></math>&ndash;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="19"><mn>19</mn></math> years of age, rather than given that the participant is at least <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="10"><mn>10</mn></math> years of age.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is incorrect. This is the probability of randomly selecting a participant who is at least <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="10"><mn>10</mn></math> years of age, given that the participant is in group A.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"89f20d9e","external_id":"edb435d2-fe23-4422-9f29-3461bdaa70a9","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"d3cd5898-69cf-4a80-9a67-3f191809b685","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"Q","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill_cd":"Q.E.","skill_desc":"Probability and conditional probability","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":7,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The table summarizes the distribution of age and assigned group for <math alttext=\"90\"><mn>90</mn>\n</math> participants in a study.</p>\n<figure class=\"table\"><table border=\"1\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 18.0583%;\">&nbsp;</td>\n<th style=\"width: 18.0583%; text-align: center;\" scope=\"col\"><math alttext=\"0\"><mn>0</mn>\n</math>–<math alttext=\"9\"><mn>9</mn>\n</math> years</th>\n<th style=\"width: 18.0583%; text-align: center;\" scope=\"col\"><math alttext=\"10\"><mn>10</mn>\n</math>–<math alttext=\"19\"><mn>19</mn>\n</math> years</th>\n<th style=\"width: 18.0583%; text-align: center;\" scope=\"col\"><math alttext=\"20 plus\"><mn>20</mn><mo>+</mo></math> years</th>\n<th style=\"width: 18.0583%; text-align: center;\" scope=\"col\">Total</th>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width: 18.0583%; text-align: left;\" scope=\"row\">Group A</th>\n<td style=\"width: 18.0583%; text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"5\"><mn>5</mn>\n</math></td>\n<td style=\"width: 18.0583%; text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"17\"><mn>17</mn>\n</math></td>\n<td style=\"width: 18.0583%; text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn>\n</math></td>\n<td style=\"width: 18