<div role="region" aria-label="Long description for scatterplot" class="sr-only"><ul>
<li>The scatterplot has 10 data points.</li>
<li>The data points are in a linear pattern trending down from left to right.</li>
<li>A line of best fit is shown:<br>
<ul>
<li>The line of best slants down from left to right.</li>
<li>1 point is touching the line of best fit.</li>
<li>4 points are above the line of best fit.</li>
<li>5 points are below the line of best fit.</li>
<li>The line of best fit passes through the following approximate coordinates:<br>
<ul>
<li>(2 comma 12)</li>
<li>(8 comma 7)</li>
<li>(13 comma 3)</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul></div></figure></p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Which of the following equations best represents the line of best fit shown?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"4b6fe541-7148-4e75-a989-b8ca91f1cf01","content":"<p><math alttext=\"y equals 13.5 plus 0.8 x\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>13.5</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>0.8</mn></mrow><mi>x</mi></math></p>"},{"id":"cd8a10ab-455a-401c-aca6-87226994693e","content":"<p><math alttext=\"y equals 13.5 minus 0.8 x\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>13.5</mn></mrow><mo>-</mo><mrow><mn>0.8</mn></mrow><mi>x</mi></math></p>"},{"id":"5b68829d-50ec-4b39-a245-520e2ce90a68","content":"<p><math alttext=\"y equals negative 13.5 plus 0.8 x\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mrow><mn>13.5</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>0.8</mn></mrow><mi>x</mi></math></p>"},{"id":"8fc8a344-73ec-4049-b8ba-00a59ec998af","content":"<p><math alttext=\"y equals negative 13.5 minus 0.8 x\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mrow><mn>13.5</mn></mrow><mo>-</mo><mrow><mn>0.8</mn></mrow><mi>x</mi></math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["cd8a10ab-455a-401c-aca6-87226994693e"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is correct. The line of best fit shown intersects the <em>y</em>-axis at a positive<em> y</em>-value and has a negative slope. The graph of an equation of the form&nbsp;<math alttext="y equals a plus b x"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>x</mi></math>, where <math alttext="a"><mi>a</mi>
</math> and <math alttext="b"><mi>b</mi>
</math> are constants, intersects the <em>y</em>-axis at a <em>y</em>-value of <math alttext="a"><mi>a</mi>
</math> and has a slope of <math alttext="b"><mi>b</mi>
</math>. Of the given choices, only choice B represents a line that intersects the <em>y</em>-axis at a positive <em>y</em>-value, <math alttext="13.5"><mn>13.5</mn>
</math>, and has a negative slope, <math alttext="negative 0.8"><mo>-</mo><mn>0.8</mn>
</math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect. This equation represents a line that has a positive slope, not a negative slope.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is incorrect. This equation represents a line that intersects the <em>y</em>-axis at a negative <em>y</em>-value, not a positive <em>y</em>-value, and has a positive slope, not a negative slope.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is incorrect. This equation represents a line that intersects the <em>y</em>-axis at a negative <em>y</em>-value, not a positive <em>y</em>-value.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$manifold$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"8baf2118","external_id":"77c322ee-efee-4f19-ad6f-03294924b08f","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":"28aca3a4-ce57-434b-96ad-ff2dbabfcf25","uId":"171e5804-96b0-4e3f-95b9-2f4e04ce5eb6","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"Q","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill_cd":"Q.D.","skill_desc":"Two-variable data: Models and scatterplots","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":3,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The scatterplot shows the relationship between two variables, <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math>. A line of best fit is also shown.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><figure class='image'><svg height=\"275.22pt\" version=\"1.1\" viewBox=\"0 0 286.56 275.22\" width=\"286.56pt\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A scatterplot in the x y plane with the origin labeled O. The x axis ranges from 0 to 14 in increments of 1, with values marked every 2 grid lines. The y axis ranges from 0 to 15 in increments of 1, with values marked every 2 grid lines. Refer to long description.\">\n <defs>\n  <style type=\"text/css\">\n*{stroke-linecap:butt;stroke-linejoin:round;}\n  </style>\n </defs>\n <g id=\"figure_1\">\n  <g id=\"patch_1\">\n   <path d=\"M 0 275.22 \nL 286.56 275.22 \nL 286.56 0 \nL 0 0 \nz\n\" style=\"fill:none;\"></path>\n  </g>\n  <g id=\"axes_1\">\n   <g id=\"patch_2\">\n    <path d=\"M 7.2 260.46 \nL 279.36 260.46 \nL 279.36 10.98 \nL 7.2 10.98 \nz\n\" style=\"fill:none;\"></path>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"matplotlib.axis_1\"></g>\n   <g id=\"matplotlib.axis_2\">