</math>% of the items are red. Of all the red items in the group, <math><mn>30</mn>
</math>% also have stripes. What percentage of the items in the group are red with stripes?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"aeb5e068-6842-451b-b204-e04b3c3f2ca7","content":"<p><math><mn>10</mn>\n</math>%</p>"},{"id":"cc993e3d-1a41-4ce3-82bd-f99bf18ba281","content":"<p><math><mn>12</mn>\n</math>%</p>"},{"id":"6e5c1add-1cb5-4efc-8bfc-338711808d76","content":"<p><math><mn>70</mn>\n</math>%</p>"},{"id":"a3dfc110-4e32-496e-9b1c-f2c88cd96a32","content":"<p><math><mn>75</mn>\n</math>%</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["cc993e3d-1a41-4ce3-82bd-f99bf18ba281"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice B is correct. It&rsquo;s given that in a group,&nbsp;<math alttext="40 percent sign"><mn>40</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of the items are red. It follows that the number of red items in the group can be represented by&nbsp;<math alttext="0 period 4 x"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi></math>, where <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> represents the total number of items in the group. It&rsquo;s also given that of all the red items in the group, <math alttext="30 percent sign"><mn>30</mn><mo>%</mo></math> also have stripes. It follows that the number of items in the group that are red and have stripes can be represented by&nbsp;<math alttext="0 period 3 left parenthesis 0 period 4 x right parenthesis"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, or&nbsp;<math alttext="0 period 12 x"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>12</mn><mi>x</mi></math>. The expression <math alttext="0 period 12 x"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>12</mn><mi>x</mi></math> represents&nbsp;<math alttext="12 percent sign"><mn>12</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math>. Since <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> represents the total number of items in the group, it follows that&nbsp;<math alttext="12 percent sign"><mn>12</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of the items in the group are red and have stripes.</p>
<p>Choice A is incorrect and may result from subtracting&nbsp;<math alttext="30 percent sign"><mn>30</mn><mo>%</mo></math> from&nbsp;<math alttext="40 percent sign"><mn>40</mn><mo>%</mo></math> rather than calculating&nbsp;<math alttext="30 percent sign"><mn>30</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of <math alttext="40 percent sign"><mn>40</mn><mo>%</mo></math>.</p>
<p>Choice C is incorrect and may result from adding&nbsp;<math alttext="30 percent sign"><mn>30</mn><mo>%</mo></math> and&nbsp;<math alttext="40 percent sign"><mn>40</mn><mo>%</mo></math> rather than calculating&nbsp;<math alttext="30 percent sign"><mn>30</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of <math alttext="40 percent sign"><mn>40</mn><mo>%</mo></math>.</p>
<p>Choice D is incorrect and may result from calculating the percentage that&nbsp;<math alttext="30 percent sign"><mn>30</mn><mo>%</mo></math> is of&nbsp;<math alttext="40 percent sign"><mn>40</mn><mo>%</mo></math> rather than calculating&nbsp;<math alttext="30 percent sign"><mn>30</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of <math alttext="40 percent sign"><mn>40</mn><mo>%</mo></math>.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$manifold$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"8cbf1415","external_id":"b90e5782-c428-473b-8c51-a587d2c330b9","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":"a6d00207-dc72-43ff-a569-e0859d605a7e","uId":"8c91c309-071d-404c-bfd6-4deb9c6f83ea","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"Q","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill_cd":"Q.B.","skill_desc":"Percentages","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":4,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p>In a group, <math><mn>40</mn>\n</math>% of the items are red. Of all the red items in the group, <math><mn>30</mn>\n</math>% also have stripes. What percentage of the items in the group are red with stripes?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"aeb5e068-6842-451b-b204-e04b3c3f2ca7","content":"<p><math><mn>10</mn>\n</math>%</p>"},{"id":"cc993e3d-1a41-4ce3-82bd-f99bf18ba281","content":"<p><math><mn>12</mn>\n</math>%</p>"},{"id":"6e5c1add-1cb5-4efc-8bfc-338711808d76","content":"<p><math><mn>70</mn>\n</math>%</p>"},{"id":"a3dfc110-4e32-496e-9b1c-f2c88cd96a32","content":"<p><math><mn>75</mn>\n</math>%</p>"}],"keys":["cc993e3d-1a41-4ce3-82bd-f99bf18ba281"],"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p>Choice B is correct. It&rsquo;s given that in a group,&nbsp;<math alttext=\"40 percent sign\"><mn>40</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of the items are red. It follows that the number of red items in the group can be represented by&nbsp;<math alttext=\"0 period 4 x\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi></math>, where <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> represents the total number of items in the group. It&rsquo;s also given that of all the red items in the group, <math alttext=\"30 percent sign\"><mn>30</mn><mo>%</mo></math> also have stripes. It follows that the number of items in the group that are red and have stripes can be represented by&nbsp;<math alttext=\"0 period 3 left parenthesis 0 period 4 x right parenthesis\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, or&nbsp;<math alttext=\"0 period 12 x\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>12</mn><mi>x</mi></math>. The expression <math alttext=\"0 period 12 x\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>12</mn><mi>x</mi></math> represents&nbsp;<math alttext=\"12 percent sign\"><mn>12</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math>. Since <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> represents the total number of items in the group, it follows that&nbsp;<math alttext=\"12 percent sign\"><mn>12</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of the items in the group are red and have stripes.</p>\n<p>Choice A is incorrect and may result from subtracting&nbsp;<math alttext=\"30 percent sign\"><mn>30</mn><mo>%</mo></math> from&nbsp;<math alttext=\"40 percent sign\"><mn>40</mn><mo>%</mo></math> rather than calculating&nbsp;<math alttext=\"30 percent sign\"><mn>30</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of <math alttext=\"40 percent sign\"><mn>40</mn><mo>%</mo></math>.</p>\n<p>Choice C is incorrect and may result from adding&nbsp;<math alttext=\"30 percent sign\"><mn>30</mn><mo>%</mo></math> and&nbsp;<math alttext=\"40 percent sign\"><mn>40</mn><mo>%</mo></math> rather than calculating&nbsp;<math alttext=\"30 percent sign\"><mn>30</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of <math alttext=\"40 percent sign\"><mn>40</mn><mo>%</mo></math>.</p>\n<p>Choice D is incorrect and may result from calculating the percentage that&nbsp;<math alttext=\"30 percent sign\"><mn>30</mn><mo>%</mo></math> is of&nbsp;<math alttext=\"40 percent sign\"><mn>40</mn><mo>%</mo></math> rather than calculating&nbsp;<math alttext=\"30 percent sign\">